NAME
       blkid - show partitions, file system types and UUIDs

SYNOPSIS
       **blkid** [__DEVICE__...]
       **blkid** **-U** __UUID__

DESCRIPTION
       **blkid** reads the partition tables and the file system headers of
       every disk and prints one line per partition:

           /dev/sda1: LABEL="PUREC-ESP" UUID="2118-8683" TYPE="vfat" PARTUUID="..."

       **UUID** identifies the file system. For ext2 it is the 128-bit value
       written by **mkfs**(8) into the superblock; for FAT32 it is the
       volume serial number. **PARTUUID** is the GUID of the GPT entry made
       by **fdisk**(8).

       With device names only those partitions are shown. A **/dev/** prefix
       is accepted.

       With **-U** the command prints the name of the partition whose file
       system has the given UUID, nothing else. This is what the installer
       and the boot configuration use to find the root partition.

       The command needs root rights (it reads the disks directly).

EXIT STATUS
       0 something was found, 2 nothing was found, 1 on error.

SEE ALSO
       fdisk(8), mkfs(8)
